    "result_text": "The full test suite passes \u2014 **34 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors, BUILD SUCCESS**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the GOLD membership tier rule: `membershipTier` becomes `GOLD` when the owner's household (owners sharing the same `householdId`) has 3 or more members after the create; otherwise the existing SILVER/BRONZE rules apply.\n\nThe tier is derived in `OwnerMapper` from entity fields only (it has no repository access), so following the existing pattern used for `namesakeCount`, I persist the household size at create time and read it in the mapper:\n\n1. **`Owner` entity** \u2014 added an `Integer householdSize` field (`household_size` column) with getter/setter.\n\n2. **Schema** \u2014 added `household_size INTEGER` to all four DB schemas (hsqldb, h2, mysql, postgres).\n\n3. **New pipeline step `AssignHouseholdSize`** \u2014 counts existing owners sharing the new owner's `householdId` plus one for the (not-yet-saved) new owner, and stores it. It runs right after `AssignHouseholdId` (so the joining owner already carries its `householdId` and existing members are back-filled) and before `SaveOwner`, matching the create-time snapshot semantics of \"after this create\". Owners not in a household get size 1.\n\n4. **Wired it** into `owners.POST.yml` between `assignHousehold` and `assignNamesakeCount`, under the existing `transaction` governance.\n\n5. **`OwnerMapper` membershipTier expression** \u2014 now returns `GOLD` when `householdSize >= 3`, otherwise falls through to the unchanged SILVER/BRONZE logic.\n\nThe new `Cp23Tests.coreGoldForThreeMemberHousehold` passes, and the existing `Cp15Tests` (SILVER/BRONZE) and all other 34 acceptance tests remain green.",
